insert into public.qa_records (coll, id, data) values ('config', 'checklist', $qa${"text":"## Client Preferences\nImage Fits | major | Always check if image placed is not cut off, should always show the main image subject\nCorrect Logo Added and Links to Correct Site | major | Make sure the logo is correct before inserting it into the business info, and if there are instructions, ensure the link is directed to the correct site they provided.\nImages/Logo have Poor Quality - Due to Designer | major | Don't use pixelated image to the site, especially for background images\nDefault/Template Site Image Present | major | Cross check template and New Build to identify templated sections/Widgets that needs to be removed\nImages Reference Client Business or Services Listed | major | Search in Google Chrome for US specific image guide\nRelevant Image to Business/Service Added to Each Page | major | Search for page service keywords for searching images in stock\nImage Orientation Faces Correct Direction/Alignment | major | If the image have face, it should face towards the content next to it\nImages With Hard To Read Text Open In New Tab | major | Image with small text must open to another tab when clicked\nDuplicate/Stock Image Present in Gallery | major | Check image gallery section for any Duplicated images or Stock images\nFavicon Added | major | Insert Site Icon using the clients business logo with 200px by 200px dimension\n## Content\nDefault and/or Template Site Content Removed/Replaced | major | Confirm all template text or example content has been fully replaced with final client content.\nContent Placement Issues by Design | major | Ensure content is placed according to the wireframe or FCD and is not misaligned, cut off, or placed in incorrect sections.\nCopy/Paste Issue from Written or Migrated Content | major | Look for formatting glitches from copying content (e.g., extra line breaks, misplaced periods, or duplicate content).\nGEO Pages Not Added to the site - CSV Present | major | If the CSV is present on the parent ticket the GEO pages/ Areas We Serve page should be present on the site\nAreas We Serve Page is not set as the Page Title | major | Page title should always be Areas We Serve regardless of the site map\nMissing Service | major | Service page was added to the ticket before designer notes and was missed.\nService Pages are not in Mega Menu | major | Site with 6+ service pages should be places in a mega menu ¶ No more than 5 in one column\nPages left as a Draft | major | Areas We Serve page should not be left as a draft when the CSV is provided ¶ GEO pages should not be left as a draft where the CSV is provided\nGeo Pages Not Setup Properly | major | GEO Pages should follow Design Resource for the Collection Table ¶ CTA buttons should link successfully to the contact page ¶ Missing content/ Incomplete content - cells are blank ¶ Duplicate Locations Listed\nMobile Draft Image | major | Mobile Draft Image was not added to the site.\nSpelling and/or Grammar Errors by Design | major | Review all visible content for spelling and grammar mistakes that may have occurred during layout or design implementation.\nBlank Pages Visible on the Front-End of the Site | major | Ensure no published pages are completely blank or show only placeholder elements; remove or populate as needed.\nContent Migrated - Includes Images | major | Ensure all written and image content provided in the FCD or by the client has been fully migrated to the new build site.\nHeadline Present and Relevant to Content on Page | major | Every page should have a clear headline that matches the page’s topic and content; avoid missing or misleading headers.\nGeneral Content Formatting | major | Verify that paragraphs, headings, and subheadings use consistent font sizes, colors, and spacing across all pages.\nDrastically Inconsistent Spacing | major | Scan the site for uneven spacing between elements, especially between text blocks, images, or sections.\nFormatting - Lists Formatted to Stand Out | major | Ensure any bulleted or numbered lists are styled to be visually distinct (e.g., with indents, bullets, and proper spacing) and easy to read.\nButton Added to Each Page | major | Confirm that every page includes at least one visible button or call-to-action (CTA) to engage users.\nComing Soon Page Configured Correctly | major | If a \"Coming Soon\" page is required, verify that it's set up properly with design and copy that match the rest of the site.\nComing Soon Page Referenced by a Feature | major | Check that any navigation or homepage features referencing a future page point to the correct “Coming Soon” page.\n1st DL in Final Content Doc. Appears 1st on Site | major | Ensure that the first design layout (DL) described in the FCD is the first visible section on the live homepage.\n1st Homepage Paragraph in FCD Appears 1st on Site | major | Confirm that the first paragraph of homepage content from the FCD is the first paragraph displayed on the homepage.\nSite Map/Navigation Follows FCD Unless Otherwise Noted | major | Review the new build’s menu structure and ensure it follows the FCD-provided sitemap, unless the client has provided updated direction.\nSocial Links Added, Correct and Visible | major | Make sure all provided social links are on the site, visible, have no contrast issues, and are linked correctly.\nFeatures Added | major | Only include four features on the homepage. Add more only if requested in the ticket.\nFDA Disclaimer/Age Verification Modal Added | major | Insert a pop-up modal for disclaimer and age verification if the content is not suitable for all ages.\n## Display & Functionality\nTemplate/Example Site Elements Present/Left Over | major | Remove all template images, colors, icons, etc. and ensure everything has been updated.\nText Color Causes Visibility Issues Including Form Fields | major | Check the text color in the form fields to ensure it's visible and passes the WCAG extension.\nLess Than 75% Whitespace Visible At Any Viewpoint | major | Remove any excess whitespace to ensure nothing is cut off from view.\nColors Pass WCAG AA | major | When using WCAG, make sure the 'AA' level is also checked or passed according to the extension.\nFeature(s) Link(s) to Correct Page | major | Make sure the features are linked to their respective pages and use the link checker extension to verify them.\nFeatures Optimized For Mobile View | major | Always double-check the features section in mobile view to ensure there is no overlap.\nClient Particulars Followed | major | Make sure all client details are complete before sending to QA.\nExternal Links Open in a New Tab | major | Always set external links to open in a new tab if they link to another site.\nOn Page Link Links Correctly or Image/Link Works Properly | major | Make sure the image does not open in a new tab when clicked.\nGMB Review Button Added and Linked Correctly | major | Use the shared link from Google Maps for the GMB review button.\nTransparent Header Causing Issues | major | If you notice transparency, ensure the text and nav are visible and there’s no contrast issue.\nPre QA Backup Added | major | After checking the website, make sure a 'PreQA_Backup' has been added.\nFloating Buttons Left Aligned | major | IF the client requested for a floating button, placement to the site should be left aligned\nHeader 25% or Less in Size | major | Make sure the header navbar size is no larger than 25% of the site and remains visible on mobile view and tablet view.\nPop-Up Modal Scrolling | major | Check all devices for any horizontal scrolling. If there is scrolling, review the text for overlap and resize it to remove the scroll.\nPure Black Paragraph Text Avoided | major | Use '#242424' for the hex code of black.\nPage Slugs Have Proper Hyphen/Underscore Placement | major | Double-check the page slug title to ensure only one dash \"-\" is used, and avoid using \"&\" or \"and\" — always use a dash \"-\" instead.\nPage Slugs Correlate with Page Titles | major | Make sure the page name matches the slug.\nNavigation Added, Visible and/or has Critical Functionality Issue(s) | major | Ensure the nav bar links are correct and that clicking them doesn’t lead to a 404 page.\nDL Links | major | Always check the ticket for requests to add a button with a link. If none, ensure the button links to the contact page.\n## Forms\nForm Notifications Configured and Configured Correctly | major | Check that the email is correct and matches the one provided in the ticket.\nForm Fields Marked as Required on Contact Form | major | Ensure all fields on the form are marked as required.\nForm Added with Headline or Description, Unless Directly Stated in Content Above | major | Make sure the headline above the form is a properly formatted text block.\nPlaceholder Text Avoided in Form Fields | major | Don't insert placeholder text in the form.\n## General NAPH\nNAPH Correct | major | No incorrect business information visible to the website\nNAPH Formatted Correctly | major | Business info should be formatted correctly when placed in the website\nNAPH Added to Business Info | major | Business info are correctly added in DUDA business info tab\nBusiness Info Connected to Data | major | Make sure business informations are connected to Data to ensure accuracy throughout the site\nAddress/Directions/Map follow Visibility Request | major | Correct Address/Directions/Map is setup in the website\nMap Directs to a Correct Location | major | Make sure the map address in the website is connected to the address in the parent ticket\n## TS App\nTS App Settings Configured | major | Make sure the business information in the TS App is correct\nTS App Color Matches Site Theme Colors | major | Use color requested in the client preference for the TS App color, Make sure no contrast issue when placed to the website\nTS App Added | major | Templated TS App embed code in Body HTML, should be replaced with the correct business TS App\nBranding/Logo Added | major | Add the Business logo to the TS App\nMain Action Set to \"Contact Us\" | major | Make the TS App action button \"Contact Us\" by default\nTS App Covering Information/Elements | major | When TS App is placed in the site. Check if it's covering any text, especially in mobile platform\nTS App Default Text Changed | major | Update the TS App Title text and description with relate to business/service offered"}$qa$::jsonb)
  on conflict (coll, id) do update set data = excluded.data;
